  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NGO Working Group on Women, Peace and Security 2025-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Core contribution NGOWG for 2025-2026.  

Denmark&#x2019;s support for the NGO Working Group on WPS is in line with Denmark&#x2019;s priority of the Women, Peace and Security agenda and promoting the participation of civil society, and the engagement will underpin Denmark&#x2019;s strategic efforts in these areas while serving as an elected member of the Council in 2025-2026. The NGOWG is a coalition of 18 international NGOs with experience in every region in the world and diverse expertise grounded in decades of work promoting gender equality. Its structure as a coalition is critical to its success, allowing it to leverage the partnerships developed between its members and women peacebuilders, women human rights defenders (WHRDs), women-led organizations and women&#x2019;s rights groups in conflict-affected situations.</narrative>
  </description>
